{#
  The uploader answers a rights claim (backlog item 6).

  Reached from the Article 17 statement of reasons, and from nowhere else: a
  copyright report that was upheld tells the author what happened and links
  here so they can say the work is theirs.

  SIGNED IN, unlike the report form itself. Whoever posted the content has an
  account by definition, and the statement went to that account's address, so a
  login proves who they are better than any token in a mailed URL would.

  Once. The link was mailed once, and a second answer would be a conversation
  this desk cannot hold; a curator who needs more asks in the normal message
  thread. The answer lands as part of the same report, not as a new one, so
  whoever decides sees the claim and the reply side by side, and it puts that
  report back on the Reports desk as open work. The next decision is mailed to
  the author as well as the claimant.

  There is no automatic put-back after a fortnight. That clock is US DMCA
  512(g), a safe-harbour mechanism we are not obliged to run, and running it
  would mean restoring something we believe is stolen because two weeks passed.

  @see docs/specs/content-reports.md §7
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block head_styles %}
{# No nonce: style-src is 'self' + 'unsafe-inline', so one does nothing here
   except tie the page to a per-request value (docs/specs/page-caching.md §3.2). #}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/page/support/report_answer.css') }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="lhero"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker" style="color:var(--trail)">{{ report.targetType.label|trans }}</div>
  <h1 class="disp">{{ 'report.answer.title'|trans }}</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="color:rgba(239,230,212,.85);margin-top:.8rem">{{ 'report.answer.intro'|trans|rich }}</p>
</div></div>

<section class="pad"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="reppage">
    {% if done %}
      <h2>{{ 'report.answer.sent_title'|trans }}</h2>
      <p>{{ 'report.answer.sent_body'|trans|rich }}</p>
      <p><a href="{{ path('messages') }}">{{ 'report.answer.back'|trans }}</a></p>
    {% else %}
      {% if error %}<div class="cerr" role="alert">{{ error|trans }}</div>{% endif %}

      {# What was claimed, so the answer is written against something and not
         from memory. The claimant's name is here on purpose: nobody can answer
         a claim without knowing who is making it. #}
      <dl class="claim">
        <dt>{{ 'report.desk.field_ground'|trans }}</dt>
        <dd>{{ report.ground.label|trans }}</dd>
        {% if report.claimantName %}
          <dt>{{ 'report.answer.field_claimant'|trans }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ report.claimantName }}</dd>
        {% endif %}
        {% if report.workOriginal %}
          <dt>{{ 'report.answer.field_work'|trans }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ report.workOriginal }}</dd>
        {% endif %}
        <dt>{{ 'report.desk.field_decided'|trans }}</dt>
        <dd>{{ report.decisionNote }}</dd>
      </dl>

      <form method="post" action="{{ path('content_report_answer', {id: report.id}) }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('content_report_answer') }}">
        <div class="cfield">
          <label for="ans">{{ 'report.answer.field_answer'|trans }} <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
          <textarea id="ans" name="answer" required maxlength="2000" aria-describedby="ans-hint"></textarea>
          <p class="chint" id="ans-hint">{{ 'report.answer.field_answer_hint'|trans }}</p>
        </div>
        <p><button type="submit" class="btn btn-p">{{ 'report.answer.submit'|trans }}</button></p>
      </form>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div></section>
{% endblock %}
